\mytriangle{red} Here you can learn how to carry out algebra with lists:
  \begin{solutionbox} \begin{center}\bf{List Algebra with Texas TI-84}\end{center}
  \begin{center}To calculate for example List1$\wedge$ List2\end{center}
\begin{enumerate}[label=\protect\circled{\color{white}\arabic*}]
\item \begin{bf}Step one:\end{bf} Press \keystroke{Stat} and \keystroke{Enter}. Type the List 1(L1) and List 2(L2) values.
\item \begin{bf}Step two:\end{bf} Press \keystroke{2nd} and \keystroke{mode} to quit from the Stat menu. 
\item \begin{bf}Step three:\end{bf} Press \keystroke{2nd} and \keystroke{1} to opperate with L1, then \keystroke{$\wedge$} and then Press \keystroke{2nd} and \keystroke{2}
\item \begin{bf}Step four:\end{bf} Press \keystroke{Enter} and you will obtain a list resulting from multplying L1 and L2.
\end{enumerate}
\end{solutionbox}
